course: dictionary
lesson: 11233
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Work is a good example. «Dad is at work» means the place where he has a job. «Work on your spelling» means try hard to learn something. It is the same word, with a different meaning each time.
explain: Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning. «The machine works» means it is not broken and does its job. «The plan works» means it is a success. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then put it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Work can also be a naming word, like a thing you can point at. «A work of art» is something that has been made, such as a painting. In maths, «show your work» means write down your steps, so your teacher can see how you got the answer.
fact: Work can be a doing word (verb) or a naming word (noun).
fact: «Work» means to do a job, often to earn money.
fact: «Work» means to try hard to do or learn something, as in «work on your spelling».
fact: «Work out» can mean to solve a problem, or to exercise your body.
fact: A combine harvester does work that once took dozens of people with sickles.
exercise: «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour.» Which meaning of work is used here? | To be broken and stop | To be made into a painting | *To do a job, often to earn money | To lie still for a long time
exercise: «When something is frustrating, a short break and asking for help work better than giving up.» What does work better mean? | Need more paper | *Are more successful | Are more tired | Take longer to start
exercise: Dad says, «I'm at work until five.» Where is Dad? | At home in the kitchen | In the park with friends | *At the place where he has a job | At the shops buying bread
test: «Show your work» in maths means what? | *Write down your steps | Draw a picture of a tree | Work out the answer only in your head | Hand in your homework late
test: Lily says, «The plan works!» What does she mean? | The plan is broken | The plan is wet | The plan is too long | *The plan is a success
exam: «Tom will work on his spelling every night.» What does work mean here? | The place where he has a job | A machine that is not broken | To do a job for money | *To try hard to learn something
